config:
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 400
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: The line of the branch bot
    accDescr: A merge into main, auto-merge turned on or off, or a required check of a pull request that fails starts the branch bot. It takes the pull requests that wait for auto-merge in the order in which it was turned on. One that conflicts with main leaves the line. Renovate builds a branch of its own anew. A branch of a bot that builds it anew, such as bot/screenshots, gets the label merge-conflict, and the branch bot starts that bot, which builds it anew from main, with no comment, since nobody has to act. Any other gets the label merge-conflict and one comment, and waits for a person to merge main into it. One from a fork stays out of the line while its author allows no edits by maintainers, a commit of it has no verified signature, or its runs wait for a person; the bot approves them only for a head that it made itself on top of commits that a person approved. While the checks of one that is up to date run, the others wait in line. Otherwise one whose required check failed waits for a fix, and the bot brings the first other one that is behind up to date, as the release app. Its checks run, and once they pass it merges, which starts the bot again for the next one.

    start["A merge into main · auto-merge turned on or off<br>a required check that fails · the schedule"]
    line["The pull requests that wait for auto-merge,<br>in the order in which it was turned on"]
    conflict{{"Does it conflict with main?<br>Then it leaves the line"}}
    rebuilt["It is built anew from main:<br>Renovate builds its own;<br>for one such as bot/screenshots,<br>the branch bot starts that bot,<br>with the label merge-conflict<br>and no comment"]
    comment["Any other gets the label<br>merge-conflict and one<br>comment, and waits for a<br>person to merge main into it"]
    fork["One from a fork stays out while it allows no edits,<br>lacks a verified signature or waits for a person;<br>the bot approves only a head that it made itself"]
    flight["While one that is up to date runs its checks,<br>the others wait in line"]
    failed["Otherwise one whose required check failed<br>waits for a fix and leaves its place"]
    update["The first other one that is behind is brought<br>up to date, as the release app"]
    merge["Its checks pass and it merges,<br>which starts the bot again"]

    start --> line
    line --> conflict
    conflict -- "yes: Renovate's<br>or a bot's" --> rebuilt
    conflict -- "no" --> fork
    conflict -- "yes: any other" --> comment
    %% The two ends of a conflict sit beside the line, which goes on below them.
    rebuilt ~~~ fork
    comment ~~~ fork
    fork --> flight
    flight --> failed
    failed --> update
    update --> merge

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class line,conflict,rebuilt,flight,update bot
    class comment,fork,failed person
    class merge done
